From a2fe006151623188fd1d7067c6a00c96a348c6ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Howard Hsu <howard-yh.hsu@mediatek.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 14:33:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtk: mt76: mt7915: fix out-of-bounds read in SR SWSD event
 handler

Problem:
In mt7915_mcu_rx_sr_swsd(), band_idx is used to index event->rule[]
(2 elements) and event->rule[idx] is used to index the rules[] array
(5 elements), both without bounds checking. A firmware bug or
corrupt event carrying an out-of-range rule value leads to an
out-of-bounds array read.

Root Cause:
The band_idx and rule values received from firmware were trusted and
used as array indices without validation.

Solution:
Validate band_idx against ARRAY_SIZE(event->rule) and rule against
ARRAY_SIZE(rules), logging and returning early on an out-of-range value
so an invalid index never reaches the array access path. Although the SR
event dispatcher already rejects band_idx > MT_BAND1, checking it here
keeps the bounds check next to the array access it guards, matching the
mt7996 counterpart.

Feature:
Spatial Reuse

Signed-off-by: Howard Hsu <howard-yh.hsu@mediatek.com>
---
 mt7915/mcu.c | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/mcu.c b/mt7915/mcu.c
index 9464a9d06..8d03b5020 100644
--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
@@ -506,13 +506,24 @@ mt7915_mcu_rx_sr_swsd(struct mt7915_dev *dev, struct sk_buff *skb)
 	static const char * const rules[] = {"NO CONNECTED", "NO CONGESTION",
 					     "NO INTERFERENCE", "MESH ILLEGAL APCLI",
 					     "SR ON"};
-	u8 idx;
+	u8 idx, rule;
 
 	event = (struct mt7915_mcu_sr_swsd_event *)skb->data;
 	idx = event->basic.band_idx;
 
-	dev_info(dev->mt76.dev, "Band index = %u\n", event->basic.band_idx);
-	dev_info(dev->mt76.dev, "Hit Rule = %s\n", rules[event->rule[idx]]);
+	if (idx >= ARRAY_SIZE(event->rule)) {
+		dev_info(dev->mt76.dev, "Invalid band idx %u\n", idx);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	rule = event->rule[idx];
+	if (rule >= ARRAY_SIZE(rules)) {
+		dev_info(dev->mt76.dev, "Invalid SR rule %u\n", rule);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	dev_info(dev->mt76.dev, "Band index = %u\n", idx);
+	dev_info(dev->mt76.dev, "Hit Rule = %s\n", rules[rule]);
 	dev_info(dev->mt76.dev, "Timer Period = %d(us)\n"
 		 "Congestion Ratio  = %d.%1d%%\n",
 		 SR_SCENE_DETECTION_TIMER_PERIOD_MS * 1000,
